statement:
Implement a quantum oracle on N qubits which checks whether the bits in the input vector vecx form a periodic bit string (i.e., implements the function f(vecx) = 1 if vecx is periodic, and 0 otherwise).

A bit string of length N is considered periodic with period P (1 ≤ P ≤ N - 1) if for all i ∈ [0, N - P - 1] x_i = x_{i + P}. Note that P does not have to divide N evenly; for example, bit string "01010" is periodic with period P = 2.

